# OksaSDR tour, "On the air": 20 m SSB in the afternoon, an English-speaking station (M7KOD POTA, 14.219): its
# voice band found in a 10 kHz view and the dial on its carrier (USB: the band's sharp bottom
# edge at the dial), checked from the picture before use (the user: the passband on the
# station, never between two). 2.9 kHz receive filter. 14.219 USB (-98 dBm), 2026-11-13 14:40.
pin 5
record 15
caption !speed 3
caption # On the air
caption Each mode as it sounds on the band right now, live from the radio.
ready
wait 4000
caption !speed 1
caption SSB on 20 m: tap the frequency and type it.
caption !mark 240,145
frequency-dialog
wait 1500
keys 14.219
wait 1500
keys <Enter>
wait 1500
span 10
wait 2000
caption Then the mode: USB, the sideband of the high bands.
caption !mark 560,115
mode USB
wait 2500
caption Phone sounds fuller with the 2.9 kHz receive filter: tap the filter width, then 2.9k.
caption !mark 933,115
popup filterChooser
wait 2000
taptext 2.9k
wait 2000
close
wait 1000
caption @ssb 14.219
caption 20 m SSB at 14.219 MHz: the station's voice fills the passband, USB with the 2.9 kHz filter.
wait 60000
caption @ssb end
caption -
record off
freq 14.074
mode DIGU
wait 2000
slices
